+"""K7 (research/K7-impl.md): the packed-scale variant of the MegaMoE fork header, as an anchored edit list.
+
+The fork header megamoe_fork/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm100_fp8_fp4_mega_moe.cuh is NOT edited on disk. When
+GRACETIER_SF_PACK is a2b6 / a2b4 / kernel-b6 / kernel-b4, fastpath_megamoe renders this list onto the header's text
+while it assembles the JIT include root; unset, the header is copied byte for byte and the include root has the name
+(the content hash) it always had. Every edit is (name, where, before, after): `before` must occur exactly once in the
+header, else render() raises and the boot stops (a changed fork header must be re-read, not patched blind).
+
+What the variant does (all of it behind one word, K7.desc, in the SymmBuffer's control tail; 0 = the stock path, and
+every SymmBuffer the host did not arm is zero there):
+  * the weight-load warp loads a routed task's scale block through the layer's own tensor map (4- or 6-bit elements,
+    one 3-D load of 256 or 384 B instead of the dense 512 B) and tells the barrier the smaller byte count;
+  * the MMA warp copies that block to tensor memory with the copy's decompress qualifier, so tensor memory holds
+    `code - bias` per scale byte;
+  * every activation scale code of the routed layers carries `+ bias`: the dispatch pull of the L1 input scales, the
+    all-token head (T <= 16), which reads the call's own scales directly today and now reads a biased copy that
+    every CTA writes before its ready flag, and the L1 epilogue's store of the L2 input scales.
+The product of a block is 2^(a + b - 254) either way, so the output is the same bits iff the tensor core adds the two
+exponents exactly (experiment E1: measured exact for a shift of 1, 8, 64 and 112) and the decompressing copy writes
+what the PTX manual draws (experiment E2: NOT measured when this was written).
+
+NOTHING HERE WAS COMPILED. The edits were written against the header text and the vendored DeepGEMM / CUTLASS / PTX
+sources named in K7-impl.md. No torch, no vllm import (fastpath modules are imported in every interpreter).
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
